{"base_rate":0.38836265223274696,"brier":0.20567131258457377,"bss":0.1341507901390644,"bss_hi":0.2550926070905684,"bss_lo":-0.034242976814773264,"chart":{"base":[565.6,70.5],"fp":[219.8,238.8],"lead":"62,239 272,216.5 482,204.4 692,186.5","note":{"base":"skill 0.13 — higher than 21% of cities","fp":"low end +2pp, high end +30pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.2 °C — better than 35% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 3%; promised 98% → rained 73%"},"rel":"64.3,453.3 189.4,411.7 500,334.9 680.3,149.6"},"country":"HK","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.2013396481732071,"ess":297.0107367863259,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Hong Kong</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Hong Kong rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 6 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>80%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>3%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 739 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 13.8 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.13, ranked 168 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(123&ndash;190) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>3%</b></td><td class='num'>136</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>11%</td><td class='num'><b>12%</b></td><td class='num'>85</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>31%</td><td class='num'><b>14%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>58%</td><td class='num'><b>26%</b></td><td class='num'>70</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>80%</td><td class='num'><b>35%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>93%</td><td class='num'><b>53%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>80%</b></td><td class='num'>227</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">6 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Hong Kong</b> <span class=\"muted\">Hong Kong</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">6 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.13</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>123&ndash;190\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>739 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Hong Kong &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Hong Kong\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.275441176470586,376.6470588235294 95.77388235294117,317.7647058823529 168.40972972972972,229.51351351351352 264.7360000000001,132.4 340.8224,61.68000000000001 387.7116666666667,23.055555555555543 411.0799118942732,18.0 411.0799118942732,21.207048458149757 387.7116666666667,63.5 340.8224,124.77333333333331 264.7360000000001,210.4 168.40972972972972,308.2162162162162 95.77388235294117,364.8705882352941 59.275441176470586,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"240.6359945872801\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"240.6359945872801\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.275441176470586,371.29411764705884 95.77388235294117,339.1764705882353 168.40972972972972,332.81081081081084 264.7360000000001,288.4 340.8224,255.81333333333333 387.7116666666667,189.88888888888889 411.0799118942732,91.76211453744492\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 3% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 136 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"59.275441176470586\" cy=\"371.29411764705884\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 11%&amp;#10;It rained 12% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 85 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"95.77388235294117\" cy=\"339.1764705882353\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 31%&amp;#10;It rained 14% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"168.40972972972972\" cy=\"332.81081081081084\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 58%&amp;#10;It rained 26% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 70 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"264.7360000000001\" cy=\"288.4\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 80%&amp;#10;It rained 35% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"340.8224\" cy=\"255.81333333333333\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 93%&amp;#10;It rained 53% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"387.7116666666667\" cy=\"189.88888888888889\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 80% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 227 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.0799118942732\" cy=\"91.76211453744492\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(39%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Hong Kong the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.05) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.27).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>171</td><td class='num'>12%</td><td class='num'>-0.268</td><td class='num'>12.3%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>211</td><td class='num'>39%</td><td class='num'>-0.022</td><td class='num'>25.4%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>179</td><td class='num'>67%</td><td class='num'>0.005</td><td class='num'>19.8%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>178</td><td class='num'>36%</td><td class='num'>0.054</td><td class='num'>21.2%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":22.27832,"lon":114.17469,"n":739,"n_cities":213,"name":"Hong Kong","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0036029411764705887,"n":136,"obs":0.029411764705882353,"sig":true},{"hi":0.22,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.10670588235294118,"n":85,"obs":0.11764705882352941,"sig":false},{"hi":0.45,"lo":0.22,"mean":0.31189189189189187,"n":74,"obs":0.13513513513513514,"sig":true},{"hi":0.71,"lo":0.45,"mean":0.5840000000000002,"n":70,"obs":0.2571428571428571,"sig":true},{"hi":0.9,"lo":0.71,"mean":0.7989333333333334,"n":75,"obs":0.3466666666666667,"sig":true},{"hi":0.97,"lo":0.9,"mean":0.9313888888888889,"n":72,"obs":0.5277777777777778,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.97,"mean":0.9974008810572689,"n":227,"obs":0.7973568281938326,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":13.8,"provisional":false,"rank":168,"rank_hi":190.0,"rank_lo":123.0,"reliability":0.06230725133207926,"resolution":0.09364605416529881,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"hong-kong","station":"","timezone":"Asia/Hong_Kong"}